==English==

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|finickier|finickiest|more}}

# {{rfc-def}} [[fastidious|Fastidious]] and [[fussy]]; difficult to [[please]]; [[exacting]], especially about [[detail]]s; [[meticulous]] and [[particular]]; grumpy, agitated, irritated until satisfied or comfortable; likely to fidget,
#: ''The baby was '''finicky''' until her diaper was changed.
# Demanding, requiring above-normal care.
#: ''The lawnmower is a bit '''finicky''' in cold weather.''

====Usage notes====
* The forms {{term|finickier}} and {{term|finickiest}} also exist, but are quite rare, and perhaps nonstandard. The forms {{term||more finicky}} and {{term||most finicky}} are much more common, and certainly standard.

